/*
 * Copyright 2026 NXP
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 *
 * System-PM constraint layer: mark which SoC power states cut power to the
 * LPADC. When the driver holds a conversion lock, the PM policy must not pick
 * one of these states. Stacked on top of the per-board overlay in boards/ for
 * the system phase (via EXTRA_DTC_OVERLAY_FILE, so the board overlay is still
 * picked up automatically).
 *
 * Every MCXN and MCXA SoC declares the same four power states -- sleep,
 * deepsleep, powerdown, deeppowerdown -- so this file is family-wide. The ADC
 * analog block loses power in powerdown/deeppowerdown; sleep and deepsleep
 * retain it. Adjust per real project characterization.
 */

&lpadc0 {
	zephyr,disabling-power-states = <&powerdown &deeppowerdown>;
};
